    "created_at": "2024-10-08T17:12:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-10-08T17:12:42Z",
    "body": "> @shhnjk: I think this is what the proposal in [w3c/webappsec-csp#665](https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-csp/pull/665) would address? If we landed that, we'd change the rules here accordingly.\r\n\r\nOh nice! Yup, that would work, though it just means that a `createScript` exists, but it is not validated (i.e. it could just be `createScript: s=>s`). But I don't have a good answer to what \"validation\" here means from a browser point of view, so I think this is a good start for V1 proposal.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
